Salesforce is designed to fix the "friction" that slows companies down. Here are the specific problems it addresses:
1.Data Silos: 
       In many companies, the Marketing team doesn't know what the Sales team is doing, and the Support team has          no idea what the customer bought. Salesforce eliminates these "silos" so everyone sees the same information        in real-time.
2.Inconsistent Customer Experience: 
       Have you ever called a company and had to explain your problem to three different people? Salesforce               prevents this by giving every employee the customer's full history instantly.
3.Inaccurate Forecasting: 
       Without a CRM, sales managers often guess how much money they will make next month. Salesforce uses real-          time data to provide accurate revenue forecasts.
4.Low Productivity: 
       By automating lead management and customer follow-ups, Salesforce reduces the "busy work" that prevents            sales and service agents from helping more people.

       In short, companies use Salesforce because the Return on Investment (ROI) comes from higher sales, more            efficient employees, and much happier customers who feel like the company actually knows them.
